            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chrisdbar"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent margarita. Nix the pre made mixes and make this with fresh lime juice instead. We used agave syrup which keeps the integrity of the drink but we prefer less sweet drinks and used 1/2 ounce of agave syrup. Perfection!",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-02T01:13:22.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marsha"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very strong so I used half the tequila. Use good tequila because this is a fresh and simple ingredient top notch margarita. I boiled the lime peels in the simple syrup which gave even more lime flavor without the tartness.",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-14T17:02:21.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Johnnie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this on the whim because I was out of limemade concentrate and boy did this not disappoint. It is so good! I only used 1 oz tequila because I know it would've been too strong for me. It was perfect! Plus, it's healthier using fresh lime juice instead of that concentrate. Going to use this margarita recipe from now on. Thanks for posting! :)",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-11T22:37:44.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Maria Bruce McMain"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was fantastic! The only changes I made were the brands of liquor because I couldn't find what was listed. I used Don Julio Blanco tequila and Cointreau. I quadrupled the recipe and made them in a glass carafe about an hour before my company arrived and they were perfectly chilled and delicious. I will definitely make again!",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-15T13:02:02.273Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "duckyjp"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make these all the time and they are a real crowd-pleaser. These are quite strong so be careful if you make a large batch and aren’t paying much attention to your pours. I like mine a little sweeter than the recipe so I round up a bit on the simple syrup. Nothing like a pure fresh squeezed simple syrup rita!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-27T19:39:51.910Z"
          },
